     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is double the maximum recommended metformin dose. The usual FDA-labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release in most labeling. A single 1700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of about 1,000 mg per dose. Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCan you confirm what you intended? Some possibilities:\n- **1000 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 3,000 mg/day, which is still above the labeled maximum.\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release.\n- **1700 mg total per day.** This could be given as 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n- **A different dose or frequency.** For example, the dose may have been mistyped.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that and give me a clinical rationale for the order note. I'd still recommend checking with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
